rd from an Iranian who has the  death sentence hanging over their head  you're a neuroscientist can you tell us  what that does to a person  good morning  um well you see the theme of the world  day this year is that penalty a road  paved by torture and as we could hear  also from what  um this prisoners said  life changes completely we have talked  to many death row prisoners they are  traumatized for for the rest of their  life as long as it takes we know the  situation in the on the death row is uh  um a disaster and beside that the  process of being sentenced to that in  Iran very often people are sentenced to  that based on confessions extracted by  torture so so  um I don't think we can actually  understand how it feels to be to be on a  death row  how difficult is it to compile  information about the use of the death  penalty in Iran  well um Iranian authorities Do not  announce all the executions so uh this  morning we published a report showing  that at least  428 people have been executed in Iran so  far in 2022 it's 89 percent increase  authorities announced only 12 percent of  these executions so about 88 percent  have been documented and confirmed by  Iran human rights it's very difficult  but after about 15 years of monitoring  the death penalty we have a broad  Network enabling us to document and to  confirm cases so what we do we we get it  from live  eyewitnesses other prisoners people  within the system families lawyers but  it is difficult and Reporting about that  penalty is illegal and the person doing  that can be sentenced to heavy prison or  even death sentence  okay I just want to repeat that figure  you gave us 428 executions so far this  year you're calling that an 89 increase  on the year before  um assuming that this information is  correct why would you why do you think  that executions in Iran are increasing  to that degree  this is the the number that we have  managed to confirm through two  independent sources and you see uh our  research of the death penalty Trends in  the last 15 years shows that despite the  fact that most people executed are  charged with the charges like a homicide  or drug trafficking the timing of the  executions are very uh closely related  to political events when the authorities  fear protests they increase the number  of executions so it seems that the  authorities have been expecting protests  in 2022 and and we believe that their  aim has been to create fear in the  society to prevent protests but  obviously they have failed you can also  see in other countries you know the  pictures that we have from daesh Isis  when they took over Syria and Iraq is  the picture of mass executions because  death penalty is the main instrument of  creating fear and political oppression  for any dictator  Professor thank you very much for  talking with us that was Professor  Mahmoud Amiri mogadam director of the  NGO Iran human rights
 

